{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-202268-r4613357","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Dutch Oven Beans","sourcePageId":202268,"sourceRevision":"4613357","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-01-24T03:57:17Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Dutch%20Oven%20Beans&oldid=4613357","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:41:43.697Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baked recipes","Category:Camping recipes","Category:Gluten-free recipes","Category:Inexpensive recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:North American recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for casserole","Category:Recipes using bacon","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using ground beef","Category:Recipes using ketchup","Category:Recipes using lima bean","Category:Recipes using liquid smoke","Category:Recipes using molasses","Category:Recipes using mustard powder","Category:Recipes using onion","Category:Recipes using pinto bean","Category:Slow cooker recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"27a3308f6c38f61be4e5295de17ecac258173bbc9a41119c1088ed09fa2c4ee3","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Bean recipes|servings=8–12|time=1 hour|difficulty=3\n}}\n{{recipe}}| [[Cookbook:North American cuisines|North America]] | [[Cookbook:Bacon|Bacon]] | [[Cookbook:Beans|Beans]]\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]] [[Cookbook:Bacon|bacon]]\n* 1 pound lean ground [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]] \n* 1 large [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n* 1 large can (53 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]]) pork and beans\n* 1 can (15 ounces) [[Cookbook:Lima Bean|lima beans]]\n* 1 can (15 ounces) [[Cookbook:Pinto Bean|pinto beans]]\n* 1 can (15 ounces) red beans\n* 1 can (15 ounces) [[Cookbook:Butter Bean|butter beans]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Ketchup|ketchup]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Mustard|dry mustard]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Molasses|molasses]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Liquid Smoke|liquid smoke]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Cut bacon into bite-sized pieces and begin cooking in heated [[Cookbook:Dutch Oven|Dutch oven]].\n# [[Cookbook:Chop|Chop]] onion into ½-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] pieces. \n# When bacon is nearly cooked, crumble ground beef and chopped onion into Dutch oven. Cook until onion is translucent.\n# Add all the beans, ketchup, brown sugar, mustard, molasses, and Worcestershire sauce. Stir mixture.\n# Heat to a [[Cookbook:Simmer|simmer]] and let bubble lightly for 10 or 15 minutes or as long as you can stand it.\n# Stir in liquid smoke.\n# Taste and adjust with additional ketchup, brown sugar, mustard, molasses, and Liquid Smoke or whatever it takes.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* About two dozen charcoal briquettes, started earlier until covered with white ash, with a dozen below and a dozen on top of the Dutch oven should bear sufficient heat. If dried beans are used, many more will be needed over the hours, as the original briquettes are exhausted.\n* Crowder peas or black-eyed peas may also be used.\n* If dried beans are used, add 12 cups of soaked beans to cooked bacon, hamburger, and onions, add the ketchup, brown sugar, mustard, molasses, and Worcestershire sauce, add enough water to make a thick soup and cook until beans are soft-maybe 6 to 8 hours, longer at higher altitudes.\n* Avoid eating this for too many consecutive days or your camp mates will move your campsite downwind.\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:North American recipes]]\n[[Category:Camping recipes]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for casserole]]\n[[Category:Slow cooker recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bacon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pinto bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using molasses]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Gluten-free recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lima bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ketchup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using liquid smoke]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Dutch Oven Beans","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 pound bacon","sourceText":"1 pound bacon","amountText":"1 pound bacon","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 pound lean ground beef","sourceText":"1 pound lean ground beef","amountText":"1 pound lean ground beef","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 large onion","sourceText":"1 large onion","amountText":"1 large onion","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 large can (53 ounces) pork and beans","sourceText":"1 large can (53 ounces) pork and beans","amountText":"1 large can (53 ounces) pork and beans","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 can (15 ounces) lima beans","sourceText":"1 can (15 ounces) lima beans","amountText":"1 can (15 ounces) lima beans","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 can (15 ounces) pinto beans