ef and chopped onion into Dutch oven. Cook until onion is translucent.","sourceText":"When bacon is nearly cooked, crumble ground beef and chopped onion into Dutch oven. Cook until onion is translucent.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Add all the beans, ketchup, brown sugar, mustard, molasses, and Worcestershire sauce. Stir mixture.","sourceText":"Add all the beans, ketchup, brown sugar, mustard, molasses, and Worcestershire sauce. Stir mixture.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Heat to a simmer and let bubble lightly for 10 or 15 minutes or as long as you can stand it.","sourceText":"Heat to a simmer and let bubble lightly for 10 or 15 minutes or as long as you can stand it.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Stir in liquid smoke.","sourceText":"Stir in liquid smoke.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":7,"text":"Taste and adjust with additional ketchup, brown sugar, mustard, molasses, and Liquid Smoke or whatever it takes.","sourceText":"Taste and adjust with additional ketchup, brown sugar, mustard, molasses, and Liquid Smoke or whatever it takes.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:202268","recordId":"wikibooks-202268-r4613357","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4613357","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Dutch%20Oven%20Beans&oldid=4613357","sourceSha256":"27a3308f6c38f61be4e5295de17ecac258173bbc9a41119c1088ed09fa2c4ee3","parserVersion":"wikibooks-sections-v3","quantityParserVersion":"source-prefix-v2","license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); 